About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A Hybrid working model

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.

What does a Partner Asset Manager do at WPP Production? &nbsp;

Our client is one of the world’s most recognised brands. A global technology company who consistently delivers innovation combined with beautiful design. The successful candidate will manage the on-going production and delivery of promotional design assets for the clients’ proprietary media platforms. They will ensure all assets uphold style, technical, quality and project-specific requirements inline with design and operational standards, delivering flawless quality, every time. &nbsp;

The successful candidates will be the main point of contact for the client in APAC and should have experience working cross-functionally with the ability to collaborate with studio, creative, QC and Producer teams and be comfortable with high volume deliverables tracking and a fast paced environment. &nbsp;

Reporting&nbsp;lines and&nbsp;key stakeholders: &nbsp;

This role reports into the Operations Lead based in London. Part of a global team, you will be responsible for line management of Partner Asset Manager in APAC, and work alongside a Partner Asset Manager based in the UK, and closely with Producers, Designers and QA Testers in various markets. This role will be a 1-year contract&nbsp;

Requirements

As a &nbsp;Partner Asset Manager you will:

• Manage on-going content development and delivery pipeline, reviewing all partner assets as per clients’ visual and technical requirements and guidelines. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Identify any design asset issues, (legal technical or stylistic) and once full review is complete communicate errors to partner(s) to make full corrections. &nbsp;

• Final review and acceptance of all partner artwork and delivery upload to client asset repository. &nbsp;

• Manage communications and workflow, ensuring projected timelines and facilitating on-going deliverables production. &nbsp;

• Work closely with Cross Functional partners to manage and traffic incoming and outgoing assets.

• Ensure Quality Assurance checks and verification of assets throughout the production cycle. &nbsp;

• Report regular status updates to production leadership, escalate any production issues and proactively problem solve project blockers in collaboration with leadership teams.

• Maintain and optimise project workflow, project tracking, internal and cross-functional communications including documentation and best practices. &nbsp;

Requirements

• Experience working in a fast-paced content environment, ideally with an agency/studio background. &nbsp;

